Iterator:
 Iterator is a cursor, it is a interface.
 To activate iterator cursor in collection we have iterator() method.
 The return type of iterator() method is iterator interface.
 With the help of this method we can able to access hasNext(), next() and remove() methods.
 
 hasNext():
  It is used to check whether next object is present or not.
  retun type is boolean.
  
next():
  It is used to return the next object of iteration.
  
remove():
  It is used to remove the previous object of iteration.
  which means we can use remove() after the next() method.
  If we try to use remove method before next() method it will throw illegal throw exception.
  retun type is void.
  
 with the help of iterator we can traverse only in the forward direction.